doc:
Reindexing both indices along equivalences preserves the absolute of the determinant.

For the `simp` version of this lemma, see `abs_det_submatrix_equiv_equiv`;
this one is unsuitable because `Matrix.reindex_apply` unfolds `reindex` first.

statement:
∀ {n : Type u_2} [inst : DecidableEq n] [inst_1 : Fintype n] {R : Type v} [inst_2 : CommRing R] {α : Type u_3}
  [inst_3 : Monoid α] [inst_4 : MulAction α R] [IsScalarTower α R R] [SMulCommClass α R R] (c : α) (A : Matrix n n R),
  (c • A).det = c ^ Fintype.card n • A.det

∀ {n : Type u_2} [inst : DecidableEq n] [inst_1 : Fintype n] {R : Type v} [inst_2 : CommRing R] {S : Type w}
  [inst_3 : CommRing S] [inst_4 : Algebra R S] {T : Type z} [inst_5 : CommRing T] [inst_6 : Algebra R T] (f : S →ₐ[R] T)
  (M : Matrix n n S), f M.det = (f.mapMatrix M).det

∀ {n : Type u_2} [inst : DecidableEq n] [inst_1 : Fintype n] {R : Type v} [inst_2 : CommRing R] {S : Type w}
  [inst_3 : CommRing S] [inst_4 : Algebra R S] {T : Type z} [inst_5 : CommRing T] [inst_6 : Algebra R T] (f : S ≃ₐ[R] T)
  (M : Matrix n n S), f M.det = (f.mapMatrix M).det
